"""Document the validated comparison without changing models or integral data."""
from s01_common import *
def append(path,marker,paragraph):
 text=path.read_text(encoding="utf-8") if path.exists() else ""
 if marker in text:text=text.split(marker,1)[0].rstrip()+"\n"
 path.write_text(text+"\n"+marker+"\n"+paragraph+"\n",encoding="utf-8")
def get(data,baseline,policy):return next(x for x in data["comparisons"] if x["baseline"]==baseline and x["policy"]==policy)
def main():
 a=read(HERE/"summary.json");b=read(HERE/"native_seed/summary.json")
 assert read(HERE/"validation.json")["passed"] and read(HERE/"native_seed/validation.json")["passed"]
 seed=get(a,"kira_pool","ml_seeds");row=get(a,"kira_pool","ml_reduction")
 native=get(b,"kira_native","ml_native_seeds");trim=get(b,"kira_native_trim","ml_native_seeds");tight=get(b,"kira_native_tight","ml_native_seeds")
 text=("The comparison is complete and independently checked. The main experiment contains %d trials in %d family cases; the direct native seed-bound comparison contains %d trials in seven independent-basis families. "%(a["trials"],a["family_cases"],b["trials"]))
 text+=("Against Kira with the full stored source pool, learned seeds have geometric mean complete-process/prepared-input time ratios %.3f/%.3f, and learned rows have ratios %.3f/%.3f. "%(seed["cold_geomean_ratio"],seed["warm_geomean_ratio"],row["cold_geomean_ratio"],row["warm_geomean_ratio"]))
 text+=("Learned native seed bounds have ratios %.3f/%.3f against default native bounds and %.3f/%.3f against restricted native bounds. "%(native["cold_geomean_ratio"],native["warm_geomean_ratio"],trim["cold_geomean_ratio"],trim["warm_geomean_ratio"]))
 text+=("Against the control with seed bounds taken directly from target indices, the native learned ratios are %.3f/%.3f. "%(tight["cold_geomean_ratio"],tight["warm_geomean_ratio"]))
 text+=("Ratios use matched case medians from three repeats; values below one indicate lower time. Complete-process time includes loading, inference, exact algebra, fallback and coefficient checks. Prepared-input time excludes family and model loading. Completion counts, all resource outcomes, individual cases and operation measures appear in summary.json and native_seed/summary.json. The direct native test learns sector envelopes. The row model still acts on fixed source identities and changing target rows.")
 append(HERE/"README.md","<!-- validated-cost-results -->",text+"\n\ns20_finalize.sh runs both independent audits, summaries and all five plots after the comparison arrays finish. s21_update_report.py writes the scientific section from checked summaries and an immutable data-release commit. s22_readmes.py updates these documentation links and measurements. s23_cost_breakdown.py separates measured loading, prediction or symbolic preprocessing, solver and verification times and gives domain-specific paired comparisons in cost_breakdown.json. Frozen input hashes are recorded separately for each protocol; validation.json files bind all measured trial files by hash. The published report accompanies the checked data.")
 append(ROOT/"README.md","<!-- kira-cost-comparison -->","[Kira cost comparisons](Kira_comparison/README.md) now measure complete symbolic reductions, exact coefficient checks, model overhead, fallback, equation counts, row-operation counts and memory. "+text)
 append(ROOT/"ML_model_seed_selection/README.md","<!-- kira-cost-comparison -->","The frozen model is also tested in [Kira_comparison](../Kira_comparison/README.md), both as a filter on the stored source pool and as native per-sector seed bounds. "+text)
 append(ROOT/"ML_model_reduction/README.md","<!-- kira-cost-comparison -->","[Kira_comparison](../Kira_comparison/README.md) applies the frozen row model to symbolic target-row operations and sends remaining terms to Kira. The local rule uses the same adapter. "+text)
 append(HERE/"native_seed/README.md","<!-- native-seeding-results -->","# Native Kira seed bounds\n\nThe seven independent-basis families use their largest frozen batches, with 99 distinct target expressions, four methods and three repeats. The methods are the learned per-sector seed envelope, the one-unit-margin native baseline, that baseline with documented subsector truncation and dot bounds, and a deterministic control with bounds equal to the largest target/master indices. The learned envelope and target-index control use the same bounded default fallback. Kira generates the equations for every method and performs the exact component reduction; Kira/Fermat then combines component expansions.\n\nplan.json fixes methods, targets and limits. frozen_inputs.json records the executed sources and unchanged models. Earlier pre-execution freezes remain as diagnostic records; no full native trials used them. storage_guard_extension.json and resumption_validation.json document the later storage-only resumption: one complete family is preserved, and two interrupted family groups are repeated in full on a single node. The original 14 partial-family trials remain in storage_guard_partial/ and are excluded from the final 84-trial comparison. results/ contains every bounded trial, including its configurations, solver exports and logs. validation.json checks the full grid, actual native seed bounds and master coefficients at independent points. summary.json records matched case medians, completion counts and native equation counts, which refer to component reduction before the separately timed combination. ../cost_breakdown.json separates measured stages. Reproduction uses ../s14_prepare_native.py, ../s12_native_array.sh and the audits and summaries documented in the parent README.\n\n"+text)
 append(HERE/"results/README.md","<!-- main-comparison-records -->","# Main comparison records\n\nEach compressed JSON file contains one bounded trial, identified by family-case number, target-batch size, repeat and method. The public plan fixes 792 trials. Records include fresh model predictions or row paths, attempts, equation counts, full rational target coefficients, exact checks, elapsed time, sampled summed resident memory and archived solver configurations, exports and logs. status and complete files describe array progress; environment files identify the compute node and CPU. No temporary solver databases are retained.\n\nOnly these main records enter ../summary.json. Pilot and interrupted adapter versions remain in separately named folders and are excluded. ../validation.json binds each measured record by hash, checks the immutable inputs and independently verifies exports and row operations. Native generation on the same independent bases also appears here as two main controls; the four-method learned-native comparison has its own ../native_seed/results/ records.")
 print("Comparison and model READMEs updated")
if __name__=="__main__":main()
